<title>UK: Black Sea port of Novorossiisk reopens.</title>
<headline>Black Sea port of Novorossiisk reopens.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Black Sea port of Novorossiisk was open on Wednesday, having been shut since the weekend due to heavy swells, shipping inspector Petrak said.</p>
<p>The port which closed at 2320 local time on Saturday reopened on Tuesday, Petrak said.</p>
<p>Two crude tankers are currently alongside in the process of loading and a third crude tanker is at anchor waiting to berth.</p>
<p>Petrak also said pipeline deliveries to Ventspils in Latvia had resumed after being shut off on Tuesday due to full storage tanks.</p>
<p>Two crude tankers and one gas oil tanker were currently alongside in the process of loading.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7714</p>
